  "_comment": "Citation style definitions. Each style is data, not code, so a new style or a corrected rule never needs a change to the engine. The fields are: label, the name shown to the user. family, author-date for styles that cite by author and year, numeric for styles that cite by number, notes for styles whose long form is a footnote. inTextEtaAfter, how many authors are named in the text before the abbreviation is used; 0 means every author is named. etaItalic, whether the abbreviation is italic. commaBeforeYear, whether a comma stands between the name and the year inside brackets. referenceEtaAfter, how many authors are listed in the reference list before the abbreviation is used; 0 means every author is listed. referenceSort, the order the reference list is written in. doiRequired, whether a reference without a link is a defect. Copyright (c) 2026 KDBN (Khaled Bhuiyan). All rights reserved. SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT The Harvard entry lists every author in the reference list, which is the form most journals that use Harvard ask for; the variants that want three names and then the abbreviation are a matter of the journal.",
